Front-side write tracking for the GPU thread split, part 2: the front reads NS2 command list
segments without waiting for the back when nothing queued or cached can have written them, and
polls of a suspended semaphore acquire wait for the back less often. Ideas from Lichii PRs #179
(https://github.com/zortos293/Lichii/pull/179: LIST_FAST, skip the writer wait once the written
pages have settled, checked on the back), #243 (https://github.com/zortos293/Lichii/pull/243:
front reads that wait only for writes that matter) and #231
(https://github.com/zortos293/Lichii/pull/231: acquire polls without a drain). Written for this
core (mode 1, macros on the back), not copied.

A segment waits as before (GpuSplit::Synchronize) unless reads are unsafe, its entry has no sync
flag, it is at most 64 KiB, all its pages are mapped and unmarked in 99zzzt1's bitmap, and no page
was newly marked in the last second. Every early read is checked on the back where the wait used
to be (IsMemoryDirty, then the same bytes); a difference logs NX2_SPLIT_TRACK_MISS and turns early
reads off for the run. A met GEQUAL acquire resumes from guest memory; an unmet one skips the wait
while the back is busy, for at most 1 ms. New NX2_SPLIT_PERF fields count all of it.
